Every clinician should evaluate a risk for an opioid-related-harm before an opioid-initiation.
Every clinician should periodically evaluate a risk for an opioid-related-harm during a continued-opioid-therapy.
If a clinician uses an opioid-therapy for a patient then the clinician should periodically discuss a risk for an opioid-related-harm with the patient.
If a clinician uses an opioid-therapy for a patient then the clinician should periodically incorporate a risk-mitigation-strategy in a management-plan with the patient and should periodically offer a naloxone-dose to the patient.
If a clinician uses an opioid-therapy for a patient then the clinician should periodically review a potential-prescribed-medication-interaction with the patient.
If a clinician uses an opioid-therapy for a patient then the clinician should periodically review a potential-used-substance-interaction with the patient.
